course: dictionary
lesson: 14197
title: Old words: motorcar
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: You may meet old words in old books, and motorcar is one of them. Read the words around it to find its meaning. «The old photo showed a motorcar parked outside the house.» The photo shows a vehicle on a road, and it is parked, so it must be a kind of car.
explain: Motorcar means a car, a road vehicle with an engine that carries a few people. Today people just say car. Motorcar is old-fashioned, so you will mostly see it in books and history lessons about the first cars.
explain: A good check is to swap in car. «The first motorcar was a bold new invention.» Does «The first car was a bold new invention» still make sense? Yes, so motorcar means car.
fact: Motorcar means a car.
fact: Motorcar is an old-fashioned word; people today usually say car.
fact: «Early motorcars» means the first cars that were made.
fact: «The first motorcar» means the very first car of its kind.
fact: Motor means engine, the part that makes a vehicle move.
exercise: «The old photo showed a motorcar parked by the church.» What is a motorcar? | A horse pulling a cart | *A road vehicle with an engine that carries a few people | A train on a track | A boat that sails on the sea
exercise: Ella reads that the early motorcars were very noisy. Which modern word means the same as motorcar? | *car | horse | bicycle | bus
exercise: Dad says motorcar, but Mum says car. Which of these words is old-fashioned? | car | *motorcar | road | engine
test: «The first motorcar was very loud.» What does the first motorcar mean? | A race won by a horse | *The very first car of its kind | A sailing ship | A bus full of children
test: «Grandpa showed us a picture of an early motorcar.» What is an early motorcar? | *An old car, one of the first cars made | A fast train | A new electric scooter | A tall tree
exam: «In the old story, the motorcar roared down the lane.» What is the motorcar? | A pair of skates | A bicycle | A rowing boat | *A car with an engine
